9. testing — 'all clear, proceed' gate
    test the backend in-process, no server, no browser, no real disk.
    seams already exist: DiskPort + ConfigParserPort are ABCs, so fake them.
    what to cover, in risk order:
      - ingestion / numap entity graph (validators, dep ordering, ingest regex)
      - kb state machine (handle_start, domain select, prompt select, hot path)
      - render pipeline (hydration, truncation, hot-prompt resolver, manifest)
      - apply_file_changes (block parsing, deletelist, fence stripping)
    shape:
      - one pytest file or small tests/ dir
      - fixture factories: in-memory disk (dict of path->content), fake cfg parser, canonical workspace
      - fake disk records writes/deletes for assertion
      - the gate is just: run pytest, exit 0 = green light
    out of scope:
      - http server wiring (thin delegation)
      - frontend (display layer)
      - gpu box proxy (pass-through)
```
