11. provider model:
    Clanker's system config can declare providers.
    The auth tokens and such would be carried in another file, contained in clanker repo but .gitignored. needs to be safe, anywayy

    a. commercial providers
       - anything that speaks /v1/chat/completions (this is openai's api?)
       - user supplies base_url + api_key (or no key for local)
       - this is the "default" shape, most providers fit here

    b. gpu-box (custom)
       - the tailnet-hosted thing, local GPU
       - adds host-side control: desktop/inference mode switching, raw box management

    c. noprovider public browser gui llm offerings on the free tier
       - basically the user will use the webui to get prompts to clipboard
       - paste those into webui of providers, converse
       - copy replies which are intented for ingestion over to clank webui, paste
```

III. Items under development

9. Rework prompt rendering
    - prompt layout declares sections. the sections serves as header text for sections, and also as keys that resolvers use to attach their content to.
        § first section §
        § second section §
        § .. §

    Renderservice prompt assembly:

    a. fetch prompt layout, parse into 
        prompt: dict[str, list[Resolver]] = ['first section': [], 'second section': [], ..]
        
    b. flatten all domain / prompt & baseresolver into 
        resolvers: Resolver = [res1, res2, ..]

    c. use a comprehension to derive a list of unique types of resolvers in resolvers. order alphabetically
        order = [MultiDocResolver, RepoContentResolver, ..]

    d. for res in resolvers:
            if not prompt[res.anchor]: raise
            prompt[res.anchor].append(res)

    e. evict any member of prompt which has an empty list

    f. for value in prompt.items()
            sort list so order matches that of 'order' from step c
    
    g. declare render = ''

    h. for k,v in prompt.items():
        render += '¤¤ {k} ¤¤'
        for res in v:
            dispatch v to helper to get res_content:str
            render += res_content
    i. render should now be finished prompt render


10. Ingestion — parse `¤ action: path ¤` output format, drop `¤deletelist¤`
    purpose: model emits a single uniform block for create/update/delete; parser validates actions and routes to the correct disk op

    [ ] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py': Rewrite `apply_file_changes` to parse `¤ <path>, action=<create|update|delete> ¤` blocks
        - create / update: extract body between delimiters, write file
        - delete: zero-content block, delete file
        - remove `¤deletelist¤` section parsing entirely
        - return `IngestApplyResult` with written / deleted / errors as before

envisioned ingestion output format:
    ¤ create: path/to/newfile.py¤
    ```
    def bar():
        return 99
    ```
    ¤ path/to/newfile.py ¤

    ¤ update: path/to/existing.py ¤
    ```
    def foo():
        return 43
    ```
    ¤ path/to/existing.py ¤

    ¤ delete: path/to/obsolete.py ¤

</BL item 10 end>


- I think its time to eliminate the use of tag syntax when rendering prompts, in favour of the ¤ ¤ based syntax.

